More random information: Naming items is useful for keeping track of them.
Say you have three potions that are the same but your pet won't step on
one of them.  #name it "cursed" so you don't go quaffing it.

Another "NAME" function I didn't know about but found accidentally:
'name' means to name a specific object.  'call' means to name an entire
genus of object.  Or would that be class?
 
So, if you have several scolls called "DUAM XNAHT" and you think they are
scrolls of teleportation, use the #name feature, when it asks you "name
<object> y/n?, answer "n".  It will then ask you, "call <obeject> y/n?"
Then you type "y".  This way, every future scroll you pick up that is
called DUAM XNAHT will say "A scroll labeled DUAM XNAHT called TELEPORT."
There you go!  Instant identification of your scrolls. 

